    "RAG’s private-doc focus appears in each of the three steps: retrieval, augmentation, and generation.",
    "Private documents are encoded into vectors in the same dimensional space so they can be similarity-searched against the query.",
    "The retriever returns the top-similar document vectors.",
    "The original text chunks are stored as metadata and then loaded and assembled into the retrieved context.",
    "Chunking and using a data loader make retrieval robust to changes in document structure or dynamic data.",
    "The retrieved private-doc context is attached to the user query, effectively augmenting it with knowledge from the private base or foundation.",
