    "Too large chunks can dilute relevance.",
    "Too small or badly split chunks can lose semantic context.",
    "Poor chunk boundaries can push the most relevant chunk down the rank order, reducing reciprocal-rank and lowering MRR.",
    "You can change chunk size and overlap and re-run retriever evaluation to diagnose chunking issues.",
    "Low-recall queries can be analyzed to find chunking problems.",
    "Embeddings change how queries and chunks are represented semantically.",
    "An embedding model that fails to capture needed semantics will not match queries to relevant chunks.",
    "If relevant chunks are not among the top 5, recall@5 falls.",
    "Even when a relevant chunk is retrieved, poor embeddings can rank it lower and hurt MRR.",
    "Improving the embedding model can help.",
    "Query expansion with an LLM before retrieval can improve matches.",
    "Index choice and retrieval settings change the similarity function, ANN accuracy/speed tradeoffs, ranking/scoring behavior, and hyperparameters like k.",
